(7692410, 1260738, 91360, '<td valign="top">this was my pick for the red. After reading your comments I think you did great with this lens, although, this method refers to zoom lenses mostly.</td>', 'this was my pick for the red. After reading your comments I think you did great with this lens, although, this method refers to zoom lenses mostly.', '2021-04-23 05:05:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(7692419, 1260745, 30049, '<td valign="top">Too bad you had to get that one 10!  :-)  Otherwise you''d have a perfectly symmetrical voting pattern.  :-D</td>', 'Too bad you had to get that one 10!  :-)  Otherwise you''d have a perfectly symmetrical voting pattern.  :-D', '2021-04-23 06:24:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(7692426, 1260738, 30214, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ytshuva:</b></div><hr/><i> this was my pick for the red. After reading your comments I think you did great with this lens, although, this method refers to zoom lenses mostly. </i></td></tr></table> you probably meant to say "telephoto lens"</td>', 'Originally posted by ytshuva: this was my pick for the red. After reading your comments I think you did great with this lens, although, this method refers to zoom lenses mostly.  you probably meant to say "telephoto lens"', '2021-04-23 12:15:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(7692436, 1260547, 30214, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ytshuva:</b></div><hr/><i> my pick for the challenge. perfect model you got there! :) . sometimes, we are planning to create a photo and everything in the puzzle is great. </i></td></tr></table> my experience as a street photographer taught me to keep my eyes open and react quickly as the opportunity to take a shot presents itself ))</td>', 'Originally posted by ytshuva: my pick for the challenge. perfect model you got there! :) . sometimes, we are planning to create a photo and everything in the puzzle is great.  my experience as a street photographer taught me to keep my eyes open and react quickly as the opportunity to take a shot presents itself ))', '2021-04-23 12:52:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(7692442, 1260738, 4008, '<td valign="top">So this is just an edited shallow depth of field image and not done according to the Brenizer method? Should that not be ground for disqualification?</td>', 'So this is just an edited shallow depth of field image and not done according to the Brenizer method? Should that not be ground for disqualification?', '2021-04-23 15:29:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(7692446, 1260638, 30214, '<td valign="top">61 images! It is impressive (I can''t imagine how long it took you to upload all of them for validation :)), but why so many? It seems that you could get away with a lot less</td>', '61 images! It is impressive (I can''t imagine how long it took you to upload all of them for validation :)), but why so many? It seems that you could get away with a lot less', '2021-04-23 16:16:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(7692449, 1260738, 30049, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by willem:</b></div><hr/><i> So this is just an edited shallow depth of field image and not done according to the Brenizer method? Should that not be ground for disqualification? </i></td></tr></table> <br/>The question is - does it look like a Brenizer Method image?  If yes, then I met the challenge.  However, DNMC is not grounds for a DQ regardless.  Only if a special rule is tagged onto the challenge would that apply.</td>', 'Originally posted by willem: So this is just an edited shallow depth of field image and not done according to the Brenizer method? Should that not be ground for disqualification?  The question is - does it look like a Brenizer Method image?  If yes, then I met the challenge.  However, DNMC is not grounds for a DQ regardless.  Only if a special rule is tagged onto the challenge would that apply.', '2021-04-23 16:46:58.000000', NULL, 0),
